{
	title: 'Commands declare their key; client-only commands',
	spec: 'Commands declare their key, and some commands run only in the client, as specified in tasks/w4/forms.md (Keys and client-only commands), which this task keeps true. Keys: /model ctrl-m, /redraw ctrl-l, /quit ctrl-c, /suspend ctrl-z, /restart ctrl-r, /new ctrl-t, /resume shift-ctrl-t, /close ctrl-w, /keys f1. Not command keys: esc (it pauses but also leaves editing the last prompt and closes pickers, so it stays a prompt key; /pause is typed only), enter, ctrl-n/ctrl-p and alt-1…alt-0 (tab switching, until /go exists). /keys looks the same as before: the same sections and order, the Tabs and app rows now come from the command list and show the command next to the key (ctrl-m, /model, pick the model), and rows that are not commands stay in key-help.ts. The keys column and the command column have one width across all sections (today each section aligns on its own, so descriptions jump between sections), and /help lists each command with its key, if it has one. The ad-hoc key checks in client/app.ts and client/tabs.ts for these keys go away; the dispatcher finds the command by key. Behaviour does not change beyond: typed /quit, /restart, /suspend, /redraw, /new, /resume, /close, /pause work, /keys shows the same rows as before plus f1, and f1 opens /keys. Tests: every command key appears in /keys; each key runs its command; typed /restart exits with the restart code like Ctrl-R; the host refuses a client-only command sent by another session; no two commands share a key; a key the browser takes is not bound on the web.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Shape: src/common/commands/list.ts (commandList: all, byName, byKey, onWeb) is the one list: name, description, category, key, clientOnly. Host files in src/host/commands/ keep only run/complete/help; a test checks the host files are exactly the non-clientOnly names. Client-only actions are src/client/commands/<name>.ts, imported by name in src/client/commands.ts (clientCommands: all, run, key, typed), no directory listing on the client.',
		"Dispatch: app.onKeys runs tabKey (ctrl-n/p, alt-digits only now) and clientCommands.key before the modal and the form, so command keys work whatever has the keys (ctrl-m over a form opens the picker; before, it did not). A host command key sends { submit '/<name>' } without a draft id (the draft is left alone); ctrl-m alone sends the `models` protocol command (0x: nothing recorded). Typed client-only commands are caught in app.submit, which empties the draft first so /restart does not bring the text back.",
		"/pause is a host command (turns.stop), so another session's /pause works too. The host refuses a clientOnly name in slash.command before recording anything: 'only a client can run /<name>' comes back as a rejected submit.",
